. *******************************************************************
. * Domestic and International Remittances
. * Remittances from anyone in the last 12 months outside the household in cash
>  only. This is to at least one household member aged 15 or older 
. * We use Book IIIB TP26 (parents), TH26 (siblings), THI30 (children). As the 
> questionaire directly states these as transfers to non-residents. We account 
> for both the survey respondents interviewed and people not interviewed via th
> e proxy as they still are a part of the household. 
. * Cash only means money for health, school tuition, or any other money. Food/
> clothes and time are not included
. * Also we only look at the receiving end of variables as we care about indivi
> duals who have received remittances, and don't need both sides
. *******************************************************************
. 
. * Parents remittances are TP26: tp26a/tp26ma/tp26pa = money for health and tp
> 26b/tp26mb/tp26pb = any other money. This includes mom, father, and joint. NO
> TE: cash_tp is all 0's and 1's and I will handle impute missing later. It is 
> this way bc a skip pattern causes individuals who's parents died or lives in 
> the household as skip thus they truly should be zero. Note: Same as 2005 ther
> e is no binary parent transfers, whereas 2009 has the binary parent transfers
. use "$path/hh02dta_b3b/iiib_tp.dta", clear
(VERSION (ene 19))

. gen cash_tp = 0

. foreach v in tp26a tp26b tp26ma tp26mb tp26pa tp26pb {
  2.     replace cash_tp = 1 if `v' > 0 & !missing(`v')
  3. }
